        "Figure 1: Public Health Large Language Model (LLM) Evaluation Areas [Number of Evalua- tions] and Task Evaluation Micro-F1 Scores by Model. (Left) We divide public health free text processing into three sub-domains: (1) burden, such as reports of disease symptoms, cases, morbidity, or mortality; (2) risk factors, such as environmental, behavioural, or biological contributors; (3) interventions, pharmaceutical and non-pharmaceutical. (Right) Evaluation results (micro-F1 scores) for seven open-weight LLM architectures (highest performing model evaluated from each) across the 16 tasks using zero-shot prompting."
